{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "description": "DELIBERATELY WRONG copy used by test-shared-fixtures-break.sh. RemovalPolicy / ScanRemoval: what a scan in Remove mode does. A serial that matches a non-deleted box decides directly (in the cabinet: remove; already removed: alreadyRemoved). Otherwise the candidates are the boxes in the cabinet with the scanned GTIN (when the scan has a serial, only those without a serial), ordered: same expiry as the scan first, then earliest expiry (month precision = last day of the month, unknown last), then createdOrder, then id. None: notInCabinet; one: remove; several: choose. `state` is inCabinet | removed | deleted. Box ids `bN` become UUIDs ending in N (zero-padded) so id order is numeric. The first listed candidate is the one the picker pre-selects.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "serial match in the cabinet is removed directly",
      "scan": {
        "gtin": "03400930000014",
        "serial": "S1",
        "expiry": {
          "year": 2027,
          "month": 3,
          "day": null
        }
      },
      "cabinet": [
        {
          "id": "b1",
          "gtin": "03400930000014",
          "serial": "S1",
          "expiry": {
            "year": 2027,
            "month": 3,
            "day": null
          },
          "state": "inCabinet",
          "createdOrder": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "b2",
          "gtin": "03400930000014",
          "serial": "S2",
          "expiry": {
            "year": 2026,
            "month": 1,
            "day": null
          },
          "state": "inCabinet",
          "createdOrder": 2
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "decision": "notInCabinet"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "serial match wins even when the expiry differs",
      "scan": {
